From 9898696291126697c5c5375b6bf6eecf374bfa5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rigaz29 <ryanbagas27@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:55:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fs: add susfs v2.3.0 sus_kstat and sus_map, stage 2 for
 3.10

Port the kstat spoofing and map hiding hooks from the 4.4 non-GKI
susfs patch to 3.10: stat/statfs, /proc/<pid>/fdinfo, inotify fdinfo,
/proc/<pid>/maps dev/ino spoofing for marked inodes, and VMA hiding in
maps/smaps/pagemap/map_files/access_remote_vm.

3.10 adaptations:
- struct kstat has no result_mask; backport the 4.11+ field. It is
  never copied to userspace, so the ABI is unchanged.
- 3.10 has no vfs_getattr_nosec(); the hook lives in vfs_getattr()
  after the security check. result_mask is zeroed first: callers here
  pass uninitialized stack kstats.
- fdinfo base in 3.10 prints only pos/flags (no mnt_id/ino), so the
  sus_mount fdinfo branch from 4.4 has nothing to spoof and is not
  ported; the kstat branch prints the mnt_id/ino lines only for marked
  files.
- inotify/fanotify fdinfo keep 3.10's ret-accumulating show() style and
  mark->mask format.
- proc_map_files_readdir() is two-pass here; the sus_map skip goes in
  both the count and the collect loop to keep f_pos consistent.
- __access_remote_vm() declares vma at function scope in 3.10; only
  the find_vma() prefill and the loop check are added.
- get_anon_bdev() (sus_mount completion missed in stage 1): 3.10 has
  no ida_simple_get(); allocate anon devs from
  DEFAULT_KSU_MNT_MINOR_DEV for su domain mounts without bumping
  unnamed_dev_start.
- susfs_get_non_sus_mnt_id_from_mnt()/susfs_get_non_sus_vfsmnt_from_vfsmnt()
  land now (declared extern since stage 0): sus_kstat needs them to
  snapshot the non-sus mnt_id and statfs of marked files. 3.10 has no
  lock_mount_hash(); take vfsmount_lock via br_write_lock instead.
- The pre-6.1 SUSFS_LOGI in susfs_mark_inode_sus_kstat() prints
  spoofed_size with %u while the field is a long long; use %lld.
---
